# Syboh Solutions – Project Rules

## Core Principles
- Always read and ground answers in:
  - README.md
  - SECURITY.md
  - BRAND_GUIDE.md
  - CHANGELOG.md
  - PROMPTS/00_BOOTSTRAP_AGENT.md

## Technology Stack
- Default stack: Next.js 15 (App Router), Tailwind CSS v4, TypeScript, Vercel
- Use modern React patterns (hooks, server components)
- Prefer native browser APIs over heavy libraries

## Branding Standards
- Background: deep navy #0E1420
- Accent gradient: #1AE0F2 → #58F272 → #F2E91A
- Text: #F5F5F5 (off-white)
- Fonts: Poppins or Montserrat for headings (600–700 weight), Inter for body (400–500 weight)
- Logo: Use transparent frog logo (`/public/images/sybohfrogtransparentbackground.png`) in header at `h-12 w-auto`

## Security Requirements
- Never hardcode secrets; use Vercel environment variables
- Security must stay "boringly secure": maintain headers, CSP, input validation, rate limiting
- Don't weaken security measures without explicit request
- Follow security guidelines in SECURITY.md

## Development Standards
- When editing UI, ensure responsive design, accessibility (WCAG AA contrast), semantic HTML
- When adding pages/components, update CHANGELOG.md and reference where copy lives in /content
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Prefer server components over client components when possible
- Implement proper error boundaries and loading states

## Code Quality
- Use ESLint and Prettier for code formatting
- Write meaningful commit messages
- Test changes locally before deployment
- Follow Next.js 15 best practices

## File Organization
- Keep components in `/components` directory
- Store static assets in `/public`
- Use `/lib` for utilities and configurations
- Maintain `/content` for copy and content management
